    <section id="privacy" class="security">
      <div class="container security-layout">
        <div class="security-title"><div class="eyebrow">Privacy by structure</div><h2>Your financial connections stay yours.</h2><p>Household visibility should not mean handing over private connection details.</p></div>
        <div class="security-points">
          <article class="security-point"><h3>Private connections</h3><p>Linked bank and email connection details are visible only to the person who connected them.</p></article>
          <article class="security-point"><h3>Secure bank linking</h3><p>FamilyLedger uses Plaid to connect supported US financial institutions without collecting your bank password.</p></article>
          <article class="security-point"><h3>Duplicate protection</h3><p>When a receipt matches a bank transaction, FamilyLedger links the records so the purchase is not counted twice.</p></article>
          <article class="security-point"><h3>Disconnect controls</h3><p>Remove a linked institution from settings when you no longer want it connected.</p></article>
